		{
			"name": "4. Borrow and return",
			"description": "Run these in order - they tell one story.\n\nMember 2 borrows book 3, someone tries to borrow it again, someone tries to return a book they did not borrow, and finally member 2 returns it properly.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Step 1 - member 2 borrows book 3",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const t = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test(\"it is a borrow\", () => pm.expect(t.type).to.eql('borrow'));",
									"pm.test(\"both sides were loaded from the database\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(t.book.title).to.eql('Spring in Action');",
									"    pm.expect(t.member.name).to.eql('Malee Rakdee');",
									"});",
									"pm.test(\"the database assigned an id\", () => pm.expect(t.id).to.be.a('number'));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"book\": { \"id\": 3 },\n    \"type\": \"borrow\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/members/2/transactions",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["members", "2", "transactions"]
						},
						"description": "POST /api/members/{id}/transactions, from library-design.md.\n\nThe member comes from the URL, so the body only names the book.\n\nThe book is sent as a nested object with just an id. Jackson builds a placeholder Book from it; the controller replaces it with the real row before saving. The reply shows the full book and member, because the saved entity holds real objects, not ids."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Step 2 - borrow it again (refused)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"400 Bad Request\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
									"pm.test(\"explains why\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('already borrowed');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"book\": { \"id\": 3 },\n    \"member\": { \"id\": 1 },\n    \"type\": \"borrow\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/transactions",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["transactions"]
						},
						"description": "POST /api/transactions - here the body names BOTH sides.\n\nTo decide, the controller runs findFirstByBookIdOrderByIdDesc(3): the newest row for that book is a 'borrow', so the book is still out."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Step 3 - wrong member returns it (refused)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"400 Bad Request\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
									"pm.test(\"names the real borrower\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('borrowed by member 2');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"book\": { \"id\": 3 },\n    \"member\": { \"id\": 1 },\n    \"type\": \"return\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/transactions",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["transactions"]
						},
						"description": "The check walks from the transaction to its member (latest.getMember().getId()) - following a @ManyToOne in Java, with no SQL written by hand."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
